    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="c6f0dc76-c98d-5272-a31f-3c8f637ef05b" activityNameId="a6fdc41d-caf0-54bd-a868-cef80784179e" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Milking parlour</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Milking parlour
The module includes a herringbone milking parlour 1x4 with 4 milking units, a pipeline milking machine, a milk room and the part of the building around and between the milking rooms (floor, walls, roof and doors). Lifetime of the building is 50 years.;
UUID: f09727aa-969d-3bef-a4af-c7c945810ec5
The inventory takes into account the use of construction materials and building machines for construction, repair and replacement including waste disposal and the transportation of the materials to the building site. Not taken into account were direct emission of the construction, disposal of production waste and the use of resources during utilization phase. 
Location: The inventory applies for Swiss agricultural buildings only, because of the solid method of construction.
Technology: The data of the inventory are based on one example of a typical agricultural building.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: Existing milking parlour in Switzerland in 1996: 2434 units.
Sampling: The inventory is calculated based on a solid database of agricultural buildings. 
Extrapolations: &lt;null&gt;
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_f09727aa-969d-3bef-a4af-c7c945810ec5.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
